                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>How much does it cost to start a home decor brand in UAE?</h3>
                                        <p>Minimum viable D2C: AED 5,00,000-10,00,000. Serious market entry with showroom: AED 15,00,000-40,00,000. Includes entity + product + warehousing + tech + marketing 6-12 months. Regional expansion additional.</p>
                                        <h3>Should I have a physical showroom for home decor in UAE?</h3>
                                        <p>For high-AOV (AED 5,000+): yes at growth stage. 6-18 months D2C-only proving + then showroom addition typical path. Dubai + Abu Dhabi primary. Pure D2C works up to AED 3,000-8,000 AOV.</p>
                                        <h3>Which marketplace is best for home decor in UAE?</h3>
                                        <p>Amazon.ae + Noon.com (universal reach). Namshi Home + The Home Store (broader). Retail partnerships: Home Centre + Pan Emirates + Danube Home + Homes r Us.</p>
                                        <h3>How do I sell furniture to interior designers in UAE?</h3>
                                        <p>Interior designer + architect trade network essential B2B revenue. 25-40% trade discount + trade-only pricing typical. 20-40 designer + architect partnerships per quarter. Contract + hospitality furniture separately.</p>
